Job:   086-release-designer-0.27.0-bump-in-job   (T-1306)
What:  Release designer 0.27.0: bump the version, calibrate the kit (codex, GLM-5.3), cut, commit, tag designer-v0.27.0, push
       Release 0.27.0 (minor).
       - The io panel shows a producer's ref and dataType, read-only like role (T-1304). Before, greenfield's ontology links
         (ref="nid:attr-...", dataType) were kept on save but never shown. greenfield found it on their own map; the
         independent reviewer judged the fix green (V-20261024-4bd97453).
       - The authoring kit's review findings carry map evidence, checked mechanically (T-1290).
       Nothing changes in stored maps. Notes: docs/releases/RELEASE-NOTES-0.27.0.md.
       Replaces job 085 (retired unrun): the version bump is now step 1 of the job, because a bump before the kit's calibration
       keeps the core tier red until the release (T-974 runs the release script, whose calibration gate has no bypass).
       Steps 2-3 run live reviewers on the 0.27.0 kit (codex, then GLM-5.3), a few minutes each and model time; if one does not
       PASS, the job stops and nothing is released (step 1's bump commit stays local and unpushed). Steps 7-8 are outward: the
       tag is permanent, and step 8 pushes bleeding-edge and the tag. That push runs the pre-push core tier on the bumped tree,
       about 20 minutes. Afterwards the agent tells AEF and aef-greenfield-test (version, tag, sha256, bytes), asks greenfield to
       rerun their own io check, and tracks AEF's pin.
Steps (each asks y/N first):
  1. Bump VERSION and APP_VERSION to 0.27.0 and commit (parity checked)
  2. Calibrate with codex (OpenAI): build the 0.27.0 kit, loop.sh --calibrate, record the result (outward)
  3. Calibrate with GLM-5.3 (Z.AI, opencode): build the 0.27.0 kit, loop.sh --calibrate, record the result (outward)
  4. Release gate: the 0.27.0 kit carries a PASS calibration of its exact bytes (outward)
  5. Cut release 0.27.0: scripts/release-designer.sh (render gate ON, announce ON; writes dist/) (outward)
  6. Commit dist/aef-workflow-designer-0.27.0.html, dist/aef-authoring-kit-0.27.0, dist/MANIFEST.yaml and the calibration record (outward)
  7. Tag designer-v0.27.0 (annotated) on the release commit (outward)
  8. Push bleeding-edge and designer-v0.27.0 to origin (the pre-push core tier runs, about 20 minutes) (outward)

